public class AccountRatingService {
    @future
    public static void recalculate(List<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Set<Id> ids = new Set<Id>();
        for (Id accountId : accountIds) {
            if (accountId != null) {
                ids.add(accountId);
            }
        }

        if (ids.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Decimal hotThreshold = 100000;

        Map<Id, String> ratingByAccountId = new Map<Id, String>();
        for (Id accountId : ids) {
            ratingByAccountId.put(accountId, 'Cold');
        }

        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT AccountId, COUNT(Id) openCount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :ids
              AND IsClosed = false
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            Id accountId = (Id) ar.get('AccountId');
            Integer openCount = (Integer) ar.get('openCount');

            if (openCount > 0) {
                ratingByAccountId.put(accountId, 'Warm');
            }
        }

        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT AccountId, COUNT(Id) hotCount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :ids
              AND IsClosed = false
              AND Amount >= :hotThreshold
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            Id accountId = (Id) ar.get('AccountId');
            Integer hotCount = (Integer) ar.get('hotCount');

            if (hotCount > 0) {
                ratingByAccountId.put(accountId, 'Hot');
            }
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();

        for (Account acct : [
            SELECT Id, Rating
            FROM Account
            WHERE Id IN :ids
        ]) {
            String newRating = ratingByAccountId.get(acct.Id);

            if (newRating != null && acct.Rating != newRating) {
                acct.Rating = newRating;
                accountsToUpdate.add(acct);
            }
        }

        if (!accountsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update accountsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

I did not make one `@future` call per Opportunity. With CPQ batches of 200, that would exceed the 50 future-call limit per transaction. The trigger deduplicates AccountIds and makes one `@future` call per trigger transaction.

I also recalculate the old AccountId when an Opportunity is reparented, and I handle delete/undelete because those also change the open pipeline. If your CPQ integration runs as Batch Apex, use Queueable instead of `@future`, because `@future` can’t be called from Batch Apex.

